## Forward MCP end-user identity past the Apps proxy overwrite
================================================================================

Context: Graph tools through the MCP server were authorised as the MCP app
service principal (`You are not a member of this domain's team`) even for
domain Builders. Databricks Apps overwrites `x-forwarded-*` on the MCP → UI
hop from the M2M bearer, so the documented header-forwarding design never
reached PermissionMiddleware (issue #208).

Changes:

1. src/back/core/databricks/ActingIdentity.py
   Swap to acting email/token only when the proxy identity is the MCP SP.
2. src/shared/fastapi/main.py
   Apply that swap on every App-mode request, including `/api` and `/graphql`.
3. src/mcp-server/server/http_client.py
   Send `X-OntoBricks-Acting-*` instead of `x-forwarded-*` on outbound M2M calls.
4. src/mcp-server/server/session_scope.py
   Still capture inbound Apps `x-forwarded-*` (those are the end user).
5. src/shared/config/settings.py
   `MCP_SP_CLIENT_ID` is the allowlisted MCP SP for the swap.
6. app.yaml.template / scripts/deploy.sh / scripts/deploy.config.sh
   Inject `MCP_SP_CLIENT_ID` from `databricks apps get` on redeploy.
7. databricks.yml
   `user_api_scopes: sql`, `iam.current-user:read`, `iam.access-control:read`
   on both apps so inbound MCP has a UC-capable user token.
8. src/back/objects/domain/settings/RegistryDomainSettings.py
   Prefer `request.state.user_token` after the swap for Team/group lookup.
9. src/api/routers/internal/_permissions.py
   Same token preference for domain filtering.
10. docs/deployment.md, docs/architecture.md, docs/user-guide.md
    Document acting headers vs Apps `x-forwarded-*` overwrite.
11. tests/units/core/test_acting_identity.py
    Unit coverage for swap / spoof / fail-closed.
12. tests/units/auth/test_permission_middleware.py
    Bypass-path swap, spoof ignore, MCP SP without acting email.
13. tests/mcp/test_user_header_forwarding.py / test_tool_http_boundary.py
    Outbound acting headers, not `x-forwarded-*`.
14. tests/units/settings/test_bundle_job_resource.py
    Both apps declare `user_api_scopes`.

